{"images":["data:image/webp;base64,"],"messages":[{"content":"A railway embankment 400 m long is 12 m wide at the formation level. The side slope of the embankment is 2:1. The formation level at zero chainage is 107.00. The embankment has a rising gradient of 1 in 100. The ground is level across the c/l. Calculate the volume of earthwork using the prismoidal rule with the following observations:<image>\n\n(A) 14563 $m^{3}$\n(B) 14583 $m^{3}$\n(C) 14553 $m^{3}$\n(D) 14573 $m^{3}$\n\nAnswer with the option's letter from the given choices directly.","role":"user"}]}